# =============================================================================
# caddy settings — COPY to caddy.env (chmod 600). Never commit this file.
# ONLY fill the lines for features YOU enabled. Empty = that feature stays inert.
# Caddyfile reads these as {env.VAR} at RUNTIME — never baked into the image.
# =============================================================================

# --- ACME contact — YOUR CHOICE (recommended): expiry + quota notices.
ACME_EMAIL=you@example.com

# --- SSO domain — YOUR CHOICE (SSO mode only): your oauth2-proxy public host.
# --- Used by the (sso-gate) snippet for login bounces. Ignored without SSO.
SSO_DOMAIN=sso.example.com

# --- DNS-01 provider token — YOUR CHOICE: fill EXACTLY ONE section matching the
# --- `acme_dns` line you uncommented in Caddyfile. Leave the rest empty.
# --- Comment out ALL acme_dns lines in Caddyfile = HTTP-01 (no token needed).

# Option 1 — Cloudflare (Zone:Read + DNS:Edit on your zone):
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# Option 2 — AWS Route53 (IAM: route53:ChangeResourceRecordSets on hosted zone):
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Option 3 — DigitalOcean:
# DO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Option 4 — DuckDNS:
# DUCKDNS_TOKEN=
# Option 5 — Porkbun:
# PORKBUN_API_KEY=
# PORKBUN_SECRET_API_KEY=
# Option N — your provider: add its credential vars here, reference as {env.VAR}
# in Caddyfile. Provider list: https://github.com/orgs/caddy-dns/repositories

# --- CrowdSec bouncer key — YOUR CHOICE (WAF mode only):
# --- GET IT: docker exec crowdsec cscli bouncers add caddy
# --- Then paste here. Wrong/empty key = Caddy fails closed (503) or open per config.
CROWDSEC_CADDY_KEY=
